From d2ed5a3d0cb166e8f0ce1a051fa3c3a3f4e57a69 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 13:50:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] A driver can say "do not text" without becoming
 undispatchable

A group blast reached a driver whose carrier has him on a do-not-text list.
Until now the only way to record that was NEVER_TEXT_DRIVER_NAMES -- three
names hardcoded in loadboard.js, which is a deploy, and which blocks a driver
EVERYWHERE including one-to-one.

atlanta_drivers.do_not_text is the softer flag, set from a Do not text
checkbox on the driver profile. A flagged driver stays on the boards, stays
assignable, and stays textable one at a time from a board row, an alert or the
pre-shift prompt. Only the Text a Group modal drops them. The exclusion is
therefore deliberately NOT in beginTextBatchFlow(), which the board's "text
selected loads" button shares with the blast -- those drivers are already on a
load that day -- and not in openSendTextModal(). The test asserts its absence
from all three, because "while I'm here" is how a narrow flag becomes a second
DNU.

Two things it has to get right, both of which fail silently:

- startGroupTexting() rebuilds its member list from the driver pool rather
  than reusing ratingTextEligible/rateTextEligible. Filtering only the two
  count refreshers would show the correct smaller number on the buttons and
  still send to everyone. All three are filtered.
- It blocks on the PHONE NUMBER, not the profile row. The same person
  routinely has a preferred profile and a location profile carrying the same
  cell -- 581 duplicates outstanding -- so flagging the row in front of you
  and sending from the other one is the obvious failure. Same keying
  neverTextRules() has always used for DNU. A flagged driver's DISPATCHER is
  dropped with him, or the blast just takes another route to the same man.

Dispatch mode, which is how this text reached a personal phone at all:

"Text dispatch where applicable" now defaults ON for the Text a Group modal
and stays OFF for the board's "text selected loads" -- the second is about a
load someone is already running, not a solicitation. Each opener sets it and
the markup carries no `checked` attribute. It used to: 0f6c842 ("Default board
and alert text actions to driver phone numbers") set it false in script and
left the attribute alone, so for three weeks the box read as on and was off.
The driver in this incident had a dispatcher number on file the whole time.

A member with no dispatcher number still falls back to their own cell.
Dropping them was built first and reversed once the numbers were counted: a
third of every pool has no dispatcher number on file -- 204 of 538 preferred,
999 of 3,128 Atlanta, 107 of 202 Mondelez -- so skipping them would quietly
cut a third of the drivers out of every blast. The fallback is flagged rather
than hidden: applyPhoneMode() sets directPhoneFallback and the progress panel
names those drivers, because the silence was the bug, not the fallback.

NEVER_TEXT_DRIVER_NAMES is untouched. Migrating those three onto the new flag
would quietly make them textable again.

scripts/do-not-text-driver.test.mjs drives the real modal in jsdom. Verified
red against the half-fix that filters only the counts, against the default
reverting to off, and against the fallback being removed again.

